 "notes": [
  "Step 1 parts kept unchanged: 1 Uno, 1 breadboard, 3 FSRs, 3 x 10k resistors, 7 jumper wires.",
  "Each divider: 5V -> bottom + rail -> FSR -> junction column (resistor top, FSR other leg, yellow wire) -> 10k resistor -> bottom - rail (GND). The Arduino analog pin reads the junction.",
  "Wiring follows the circuit image (the authority): the yellow wire at column 6 goes to A2, column 16 to A1, column 24 to A0. The schematic's label order differs only in drawing.",
  "Breadboard hole names use the catalogue convention: bank 't' = rows a-e (the lower half in the image), so junction columns are 6, 16, 24 with rows a (resistor), b (FSR leg), e (yellow wire).",
  "Rail hole indices (e.g. bp.4, bn.6) are arbitrary positions on the continuous rail; each rail is one strip. Top rails are linked to bottom rails by the black (-) and red (+) wires on the right.",
  "FSR legs are symmetric; port 1 goes to the junction column, port 2 to the + rail. GND wire goes to the Uno's GND.1 (image shows the power-header GND pin; which of the GND pins is not distinguishable)."
 ],
